OpenFork
========

OpenFork is a fork of OpenCode (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode),
the open source AI coding agent.

Original work: Copyright (c) 2025 opencode, licensed under the MIT License.
The full original copyright and permission notice is kept unchanged in the
LICENSE file and applies to this fork and all substantial portions of it.

Upstream:   https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode
Forked at:  upstream branch `dev`, commit 906e370146 (OpenCode 2.3.x), 2026-11-20

Changes made in this fork (summary):
- The product is renamed to OpenFork: the CLI binary is `openfork`, and the
  user-facing name in the CLI, TUI, web app and desktop strings is "OpenFork".
- OpenFork is a different window onto the same OpenCode install: it shares
  OpenCode's data, config and sessions and attaches to the OpenCode background
  service (starting the upstream `opencode` binary when none is running). It
  never replaces that service on a version mismatch.
- TUI: the header of an expanded group (activity, thoughts, exploration,
  instructions) stays pinned at the top while you scroll inside it; click it to
  collapse the group in place.
- `OPENFORK_*` environment variables are accepted as aliases for `OPENCODE_*`.
- Self-update from the upstream release service is disabled.

"OpenCode", "OpenCode Zen", "OpenCode Go" and related names are the names of
the upstream project and its services; OpenFork is not affiliated with or
endorsed by their authors. References to those services are kept as-is.
